  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Northern and central Nevada is \ncurrently sitting south of an upper level trough across the \nPacific Northwest. This setup is bringing breezy to locally windy \nconditions to the region. Afternoon high temperatures are coming \nin cooler versus yesterday with readings in the 70s. Look for the \nwinds to subside during the evening with a cold night ahead with \nlows in the 20s and 30s.\n\nMonday through Wednesday, the area will be under a dry southwest\nflow aloft. Conditions will generally be dry with light winds\nexcept for east-central Nevada. Winds across White Pine county\nwill be out of the southwest 15 to 25 mph with gusts to 40 mph\neach afternoon. Highs will be in the 70s for Tuesday and warming\ninto the 70s and 80s Wednesday afternoon. Overnight lows will be\nin the 30s and 40s.\n\nBy Thursday and Friday all models are depicting an upper level\ntrough diving to the south. This will bring breezy afternoon winds\nwith highs in the 70s and 80s. At this time, the airmass is\nanticipated to remain on the dry side. Overnight lows will be in\nthe 30s.\n\nOn Saturday and Sunday, expect continued dry conditions with highs\nin the 70s and 80s and lows in the 30s and 40s.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No changes were made to the NBM\nforecast. Confidence is high regarding cooler temperatures through \nMonday. Moderate to high confidence exists during mid-week as \ntemperatures gradually warm, climbing to at or just above normal \nconditions.",
